welcome to the final great saga of one  piece we have made it we are officially  in the endgame now the marines  demonstrate their immense power shanks  finally reveals his true face and sabo  has risen to almost as much fame as  luffy has across the world in other  words pure one piece greatness so four  terrible weeks of endless waiting and we  are finally back with fresh one-piece  contents and just how the yonko zaga has  ended with a massive bang the new loft  tail saga has just started off with an  even bigger one and of course the only  correct way to start is by addressing  the man the myth the living legend of  one piece shanks who actually has been  in less than a dozen chapters of one  piece overall in other words whenever he  is there big things are happening and  that is exactly what we've got shanks is  literally sailing in the waters of wano  just a few miles away from where luffy  is celebrating his victory with the  citizens right now and holy usopp there  is so much going on in the few panels he  gets here first of all shanks reveals  that he will not be meeting with luffy  right now not  which is hilarious because i actually  have a video coming out in two or three  days about why when and where shanks and  luffy will meet and what will most  likely happen i said that this meeting  is going to happen very soon most likely  on elbaf then it was rumored that shanks  was going to be in this chapter close to  wano so i changed the script only to  read it and find out that he's only  doing a kind of drive-by around wano  which as you can imagine gave me a bit  of a headache anyways i have a full  video about what will happen between  luffy and shanks very soon so make sure  to subscribe if you don't want to miss  that it's gonna blow your mind i promise  but for now let's focus on the chapter i  think we just all have to accept that  the kind and funny things that we got to  know in early one ps is long gone as we  have learned throughout the story with  shanks stopping kaido stopping the war  meeting the gorosei and so on and so  forth and as this chapter confirms  shanks is one of the most powerful  pirates in the world and a master  manipulator he has been pulling the  strings and guided the events of the one  piece world from behind the scenes  competing with the likes of blackbeard  and the world government to prepare for  his dream of the future whatever that  might be honestly i always took shanks  to be more of a pacifist someone who  would try to avoid battle if somewhat  possible he doesn't fight higuma until  he threatens luffy he stopped kaido from  turning the ward marine fort into the  apocalypse basically he stopped the war  completely and overall it felt like he  was a pretty peace loving guy with  enough power to back that up and i think  that's also what gave shanks a bit of a  bad reputation among fans with many  theorizing that shanks might be the  weakest yonko and only has reached his  level through some sort of trick or  manipulation as well well i think that  this chapter has now turned this belief  completely on its head shanks comes  across here as colts calculated and very  very much willing to fight it turns out  that he indeed has a number of  territories in the new world just like  all the other yonko and that bartolomeo  burning his flag and replacing it with  luffy's will have some very serious  repercussions for him to say the least  as many people have predicted shanks is  seriously coming for his head and he  doesn't sound all too happy that he  works under luffy i need to take care of  my credibility damn this really gave me  shivers i'm not gonna lie shanks is the  real deal and bartolomeo is in some  serious trouble and as if this weren't  enough already shanks also announces  that it's time to join the fight for the  one piece no more standing by and  letting things develop shanks will now  take the stage and actively participate  no wonder that oda and his staff are so  excited for film rats as am i this  sounds like there is a lot of conflict  between luffy and shanks luffy's  underling basically stole one of  shanks's islands and now he tells ben  beckman it's time to join the fight for  the one piece a battle between the four  yonko four love tale luffy shanks buggy  and blackbeard and so all of this of  course brings up the old question  whether shanks might not actually be the  bad guy in disguise again wait for my  video in a few days but i think one  really important hint that we get in  this chapter in particular are shanks's  men they are over the moon to read the  news about luffy defeating kaido they're  all dying to meet luffy in a really  positive way lucky roo bong punch lime  juice they all are excited to finally  reunite with the boy that they met so  many years ago and had so much fun with  to me this indicates that shanks also  doesn't shut up about luffy all the time  either that all of the red hat pirates  have been eager to meet luffy for years  they all truly seem to be luffy's  friends here they are surprised by  shane's not wanting to meet luffy right  now as we are and so i think shanks  acting this way is really just oda  sensei knowing exactly how to play with  us by leaving this ambiguous on purpose  because really the only way that shanks  could turn out to be a bad guy i think  is if he had also fooled his entire crew  which yes is not impossible but also not  exactly likely and so i want shanks to  be the secret weapon that luffy can rely  on in the ends then again if shanks  actually does turn out to be only using  luffy and that he's mostly in it for  himself or some other motive i wouldn't  be mad at all either just so we get that  out of the way in truth if i had to bet  money on it the reality probably falls  somewhere between the two shanks is an  ally and does care for luffy but he has  a higher hidden motive as well that  comes before that i think shanks might  well turn out to be one of the most  morally complex and interesting  characters in the entire story at the  end i also absolutely love that little  flashback to the very first chapter of  the story that we get and a look at  shanks stealing the nika fruit i mean it  was already pretty much obvious that  shanks knew exactly what he was doing  there and what that fruit truly was but  it's nonetheless giving me goosebumps  seeing it drawn and how he reacts to  luffy's awakening it's almost as if  luffy awakening the nika fruit was the  signal that shanks has been waiting for  to launch the race for lovetail and of  course i am incredibly excited to  finally see the red hair pirates in  actions especially lucky roo and ben  beckman and i love that yasob is not  emotionally prepared to face his son yet  that he abandoned as a kid back in her  village like the most heartless father  there is i also want to remind you that  no one not a single man in shanks's crew  has eaten a devil fruit for some  mysterious reason most likely related to  the one piece in other words this is a  yonko crew purely based on power and  skill alone which is really as  impressive as it gets if we're being  honest the only thing that's mysterious  now and that i'm really curious about is  why shanks was hanging around wano in  the first place if it wasn't to see  luffy did he come for pluton however  what i think is even more likely is  actually that shanks has come for  kaido's poneglyph after all shanks  himself hasn't been to love tale before  so maybe he still needed that one for  his collection too that would actually  make a ton of sense now that i think  about it and what would be even more  hilarious of course if shanks didn't  possess the last poneglyph after all but  now has kaidos because the straw hats  were too slow to actually get it someone  else who has made use of kaido's defeat  and is very much eager to meet luffy in  person on the other hand is green bull i  still really can't shake the feeling  that he might actually be from wano  himself i went to detail on that in this  video right here but this chapter  focuses mostly on him being even more of  a beast than we have already seen last  chapter kinemon and the remaining  scabbards notice him moving towards the  capital and decide to stop him before he  can disturb luffy and the straw hats and  so ryokugyu really hits home the fact  that he's kind of a douche he gives  kinemon and ko a big speech about the  world order and how you need to  discriminate in order to make the world  work for the celestial dragons that is  of course  sounds like he's rejecting a little bit  there maybe however the power that he  unleashes is absolutely ridiculous and  the real deal i really don't want to  know how crazy a battle between two of  the admirals might really look this is  just ridiculous actually scratch that  there is nothing i want to see more  right now than seeing two admirals i  actually made the argument in my green  bull video that aramaki might very well  be a logia fruit user which surprisingly  is confirmed right now one chapter later  the fact that he calls himself a force  of nature and compares his forest  abilities to the sea raises two  incredibly interesting possibilities for  me as well one since greenville falls in  line with all the other admiral devil  fruit powers i think we should assume  that fujitora's devil fruit also is a  logia though i really couldn't tell you  how that would make any sense but it  seems very likely now and two aramaki  has just pushed the door wide open for a  sea logia devil fruit like i can't be  the only one that takes this line as  some possible foreshadowing for this  right the ultimate devil fruit possibly  in the possession of emu whose name as  you'll remember is umi in return which  literally is the word for ocean in  japanese i think this theory has gotten  quite a boost with this statement then  yamato and momo step in hands oh boy all  the people who doubted where yamato  would be ranked inside the straw hats i  think it's pretty close to the top the  fact that she can knock this monster  down like this and the ryokugyu mentions  how powerful her haki is really warms my  heart yamato has really become my  favorite character in the series  together with zorro at least maybe even  a tiny little bit more and seeing her  handing it to one of the most powerful  people in the world is just so  satisfying to me i'm of course really  curious to see how momo will hold up  against him one versus one as well momo  has grown a lot throughout the raid on  onigashima physically and mentally but  as his failed border breath shows us he  is far from actually being on kaido's  level with his devil fruit and then  there is of course the entire sabo  situation and it is really reassuring to  hear that it was cobra after all and not  vivi that has been killed and that sabo  has not been captured to start a second  round of marineford and i'm really  fascinated by this new character we're  introduced to head of the marine  criminal investigation server's kudo uma  which means black horse and not only  does this introduce an entirely new  branch of the marines to us but i'm very  much intrigued by the fact that this man  follows the naming scheme of the other  admiral in other words color plus animal  black horse red dog and so on and so  forth correct me if i'm wrong but it  does sound a lot to me like oda sensei  just dropped another admiral level  character out of nowhere into the story  and i'm of course all for it the real  question of course now is what has  happened to sabo and vivi but luckily  for you you don't have to wonder about  that at all because i have already made  an entire video about exactly that that  seems to have hit the nail pretty much  on its head
 

